1
00:00:01,820 --> 00:00:06,760
Alchemy, the science of understanding,
deconstructing, and reconstructing matter.

2
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:09,880
However, it is not an all-powerful art.

3
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:12,820
It is impossible to create
something out of nothing.

4
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:17,320
If one wishes to obtain something,
something of equal value must be given.

5
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:21,500
This is the law of equivalent exchange,
the basis of all alchemy.

6
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:24,980
In accordance with this law,
there is a taboo among alchemists.

7
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:27,580
Human transmutation is strictly forbidden.

8
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:30,860
For what could equal the value
of a human soul?

9
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:34,760
Kono omoi wo keshite shimau niwa

10
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:37,100
mada jinsei nagai dsho?

11
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:43,540
Yarinokoshite'ru koto
yarinaoshite mitai kara

12
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:59,540
Yume no tsuzuki oikakete ita hazu na no ni

13
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:05,880
Magarikunetta
hosoi michi hito ni tsumazuku

14
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:12,800
Ano koro mitai ni tte modoritai wake ja nai ni
Nakushite kita sora wo sagashite'ru

15
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:14,420
Wakatte kuremasu you ni

16
00:01:14,420 --> 00:01:19,580
Gisei ni natta you na
kanashii kao wa yamete yo

17
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:23,040
Tsumi no saigo wa namida ja nai yo
Zutto kurushiku seotte'ku n da

18
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:26,420
Deguchi mienai kanjou meiro ni
dare wo matte'ru no?

19
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:30,000
Shiroi nooto ni tsuzutta you ni
motto sunao ni hakidashitai yo

20
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,140
Nani kar nogaretai n da
genjitsu tte yatsu?

21
00:01:33,140 --> 00:01:39,840
Kanaeru tame ni ikite'ru n datte
Sakebitaku naru yo Kikoete imasu ka?

22
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:44,940
Bunai n nante yatte'rarenai kara

23
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:46,820
...kaeru basho mo nai no

24
00:01:46,820 --> 00:01:50,120
Yasashisa niwa itsumo kansha shite'ru

25
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:53,600
Dakara tsuyoku naritai
(I'm on the way)

26
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:57,260
Natsukashiku naru
konna itami mo kangei jan

27
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:06,380
God's children, who live upon this land,
pray in faith and ye shall be saved.

28
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:10,480
Those who have lost their way,
the Sun God Leto shall shine...

29
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:13,790
So what are you guys,
like street performers or something?

30
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:17,040
Seriously?! Do we look like
street performers to you?

31
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:19,180
Yeah, that's why I asked!

32
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:20,480
Let's go, Al.

33
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:21,780
RADIO: ...I am an Emmisary of the Sun God Leto...

34
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:23,780
Hey! Easy!
I didn't mean nothing by it.

35
00:02:24,780 --> 00:02:27,140
Sorry, accident. We'll fix it!

36
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:28,760
How's that? It's smashed to hell!

37
00:02:28,890 --> 00:02:30,510
Watch and learn, gramps.

38
00:02:32,660 --> 00:02:34,390
Okay, here goes!

39
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:40,440
[TWINKLING]
There, see. How's that?

40
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:44,860
Amazing, it's a miracle! You've been touched
by the Sun God just like Father Cornello!

41
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:46,360
Touched by who now?

42
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:48,440
It's not a miracle, it's alchemy!

43
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:50,820
Oh, so you two are alchemists.
Right, I've heard of them!

44
00:02:50,860 --> 00:02:53,460
Then maybe you've heard of us!
We're the Elric Brothers.

45
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:55,160
The Elric Brothers, you say?

46
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:56,920
Right...I do know that name!

47
00:02:56,920 --> 00:02:59,900
The Fullmetal Alchemist,
Edward Elric, is that right?

48
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:03,210
[ED CHUCKLING]
Wow, so you're the young prodigy
they tell all the stories about?

49
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:05,420
You've grown so much!
Look at the armor!

50
00:03:05,420 --> 00:03:07,540
That must be how he got
the name Fullmetal!

51
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:09,780
Uh...no! Um...
It's not me!

52
00:03:09,880 --> 00:03:11,020
ENTIRE CROWD:
...Huh?

53
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:14,880
What? You mean it's
the little guy there?

54
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:18,080
Who's little?! Come here
and say that to my face I dare ya!

55
00:03:20,770 --> 00:03:23,800
...Lift thy voice to God...
ED: So, what's with this guy on the radio?

56
00:03:23,820 --> 00:03:27,320
T-That's our leader, Father Cornello.

57
00:03:27,820 --> 00:03:32,400
We were lost until he came to town and
began teaching us all the ways of the Sun God Leto...

58
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:36,520
He grants eternal life to the souls of the faithful...
He can even resurrect the dead...

59
00:03:36,580 --> 00:03:39,830
His miracles are proof that
what he says is true!

60
00:03:39,920 --> 00:03:42,720
So this guy's claiming he
can bring the dead back to life?

61
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:44,720
Now that's something I gotta see.

62
00:03:45,170 --> 00:03:49,760
[CROWD CHEERING]

63
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:58,260
[CROWD CHEERING]
Praise Leto!

64
00:03:58,260 --> 00:04:01,120
ED: So that's it, huh?
What do you think?

65
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:04,770
There's nothing to  think!
That's alchemy, no doubt about it.

66
00:04:05,040 --> 00:04:07,840
ED: But somehow he's ignoring the
law of equivalent exchange.

67
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:11,760
He should've only been able to transmute
that flower into an object of equal mass.

68
00:04:11,820 --> 00:04:14,950
AL: And he's changing organic matter
into inorganic matter.

69
00:04:15,030 --> 00:04:17,220
He shouldn't be able to do that...
Unless...

70
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:19,560
ED: Yeah, there's just one way...

71
00:04:19,960 --> 00:04:21,540
Bingo!

72
00:04:21,540 --> 00:04:25,600
[CHURCH BELLS RINGING]

73
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:34,780
O merciful God, please hear me.
Hear my prayer, I beg of you.

74
00:04:35,550 --> 00:04:36,700
Please bring him back—

75
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:39,260
Huh, so this is the almighty Leto?

76
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:42,180
Welcome! Are you interested
in Letoism?

77
00:04:42,270 --> 00:04:45,340
Nope, can't say I am.
Not really the religious type.

78
00:04:46,110 --> 00:04:50,650
Well, I'm sorry to hear that.
To know God is to know hope.

79
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:55,570
If we believe in divine grace...
Then through Him, all things are possible.

80
00:04:55,660 --> 00:04:57,060
If you believed...

81
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:59,820
I'm sure Leto would bless you
and make you grow taller!

82
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:00,040
Translation: "Sincere"
I'm sure Leto would bless you
and make you grow taller!

83
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:01,780
What's that supposed to mean?!
Translation: "Sincere"

84
00:05:01,780 --> 00:05:03,800
Easy, brother,
she's just trying to help!
Translation: "Sincere"

85
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:07,040
[SIGHS] What about bringing
the dead back to life?

86
00:05:07,620 --> 00:05:09,460
Do you believe that's possible, too?

87
00:05:09,550 --> 00:05:10,540
Yes.

88
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:12,240
[SIGHS]

89
00:05:14,010 --> 00:05:17,220
Water, 35 liters; carbon, 20 kilograms;

90
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:21,020
ammonia, 4 liters; lime, 1 .5 kilograms;

91
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:23,980
phosphorus, 800 grams; salt, 250 grams;

92
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:27,280
saltpeter, 100 grams, and various other trace elements.

93
00:05:27,440 --> 00:05:28,300
Huh?

94
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:34,360
That list represents the complete chemical makeup
of the human body for the average adult.

95
00:05:34,450 --> 00:05:37,260
It's been calculated to
the last microgram, but still,

96
00:05:37,340 --> 00:05:41,020
There's never been one reported case
of successfully creating a human life.

97
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:45,280
And you're telling me something modern science
can't do, you can do with prayer?!

98
00:05:45,370 --> 00:05:47,220
Lift thy voice to God!

99
00:05:47,460 --> 00:05:49,840
And the prayers of the faithful
shall be answered!

100
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:52,580
Did I mention?
All those ingredients I read off...

101
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:56,600
Down at the market a kid could buy every
one of them for the spare change in his pocket.

102
00:05:56,970 --> 00:05:59,680
As it turns out,
humans are pretty cheap.

103
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:02,520
No, that's blasphemy!
People are...

104
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:04,220
We are all children of God!

105
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:05,820
Created in His image!

106
00:06:05,820 --> 00:06:06,980
[ED CHUCKLES]

107
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:10,110
You have to understand,
alchemists are scientists.

108
00:06:10,190 --> 00:06:14,150
We don't believe in unprovable concepts
like creators or gods.

109
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:16,860
We observe the physical laws
that govern this world...

110
00:06:16,950 --> 00:06:18,860
To try to learn the truth.

111
00:06:19,340 --> 00:06:20,840
It's ironic, really.

112
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:24,880
That through the application of science,
we have in many ways been given the power to...

113
00:06:24,880 --> 00:06:26,540
[CHUCKLES]
...play gods ourselves.

114
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:30,920
So you're putting yourself on the same
level as God?! That's just...sheer arrogance!

115
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,000
You know, there's an old myth...

116
00:06:33,090 --> 00:06:35,700
About a hero who
flew on wings made of wax.

117
00:06:35,960 --> 00:06:38,900
He thought he could touch the sun,
but when he got too close...

118
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:42,140
His wings melted and he came
crashing back down to Earth.

119
00:06:42,140 --> 00:06:43,660
Right, Al?

120
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:44,680
AL: Brother...

121
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:48,020
I'm sorry, Miss,
this is difficult for me to ask,

122
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:52,440
But do you think your Father Cornello could
even save an arrogant scientist, like me?

123
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:54,240
Of course, that's wonderful!

124
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:56,920
If anyone can lead you
to the Creator's light, he can!

125
00:06:57,950 --> 00:07:01,410
Father Cornello, there are visitors here
who wish to see you.

126
00:07:01,490 --> 00:07:03,740
A child, and a man
wearing a suit of armor.

127
00:07:03,740 --> 00:07:06,200
They would only give their names
as "the Elric Brothers".

128
00:07:06,290 --> 00:07:08,780
I can't be bothered right now,
just send them away.

129
00:07:09,180 --> 00:07:12,200
Wait! The Elrics? You're sure that's
what they said? You're positive?

130
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:14,840
Yes, Father, that's what they
called themselves. No mistake.

131
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:16,720
Damn!
Then this is a problem.

132
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:19,880
Edward Elric, the Fullmetal Alchemist,
has come to call on us.

133
00:07:19,970 --> 00:07:21,720
That's him?!
The man in the armor?

134
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:23,800
Mmm. Dressing the part,
it would seem.

135
00:07:23,890 --> 00:07:26,600
But why would a State Alchemist
be here in Liore?

136
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:29,270
Surely they can't have
found out about our plans?

137
00:07:29,350 --> 00:07:33,190
It's possible this dog's nose
is too sharp for his own good.

138
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:36,110
This way, please.

139
00:07:36,190 --> 00:07:39,260
Father Cornello is a busy man,
as you can imagine.

140
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:42,220
But you're in luck,
he's decided to spare a moment for you.

141
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:46,160
Yeah, thanks! We understand,
we won't take too much of his time.

142
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:47,490
Good, then it's agreed.

143
00:07:47,580 --> 00:07:49,750
We'll make this quick.

144
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:54,380
Brother Cray, what is this?
What do you think you're doing?!

145
00:07:54,470 --> 00:07:58,590
Rose, these heathens have come to ensnare
and discredit the Father. They're evil.

146
00:07:58,670 --> 00:07:59,880
This is God's will.

147
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:00,880
Brother Cray...!

148
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:04,320
Well, like you said,
let's make this quick!

149
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:08,640
[GASPS]

150
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:14,980
Oh yeah, strike!

151
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:17,020
What's this commotion?

152
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:23,120
Ah, the Fullmetal Alchemist. Welcome
to the home of our sacred order.

153
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:25,120
Father Cornello!

154
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:27,840
CORNELLO: I must apologise
for my disciples' behavior.

155
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:29,840
It would seem they've
been misguided.

156
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:33,460
ED: Okay, let's say I believe you weren't
the one guiding them. What next?

157
00:08:33,620 --> 00:08:35,640
Have you come to learn
the ways of Leto?

158
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:37,840
Well there are a few things
I'm curious about.

159
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:41,540
Like how you've been using
second-rate alchemy to deceive your followers.

160
00:08:41,540 --> 00:08:42,180
[GASP]

161
00:08:42,180 --> 00:08:44,180
My dear boy,
I don't know what you mean.

162
00:08:44,260 --> 00:08:47,960
What your doubting eyes see as alchemy
are the miracles of the Sun God Leto.

163
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:52,620
Look again. Could mere alchemy create
something from nothing in this way?

164
00:08:53,190 --> 00:08:55,240
ED: Yeah, that's
what I didn't get at first.

165
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:59,880
How can you perform transmutations
that ignore the law of equivalent exchange?

166
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:02,110
As I said,
because it isn't alchemy!

167
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:04,400
But then I started thinking about it...

168
00:09:04,490 --> 00:09:08,540
If you'd somehow managed to acquire
a certain object to amplify your alchemy...

169
00:09:08,540 --> 00:09:11,340
One that's said to
make the impossible possible...

170
00:09:11,340 --> 00:09:13,290
That would explain everything.

171
00:09:13,290 --> 00:09:14,080
What?!

172
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:17,130
I'm talking about
the Philosopher's Stone.

173
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:19,460
Your ring, that's it,
isn't it?

174
00:09:21,260 --> 00:09:23,260
I've been looking for that.

175
00:09:23,260 --> 00:09:24,800
The ring is just a ring.

176
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:28,640
I am God's humble servant,
it is from he alone that I derive my power.

177
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:30,640
Still trying to sell that line, huh?

178
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:34,810
If that's the way you wanna play it, I guess I'll have
to come up there and beat some truth out of ya.

179
00:09:34,890 --> 00:09:38,060
My, you really are quite
the incorrigible heathen, aren't you?

180
00:09:38,150 --> 00:09:39,190
Rose, dear?

181
00:09:39,270 --> 00:09:40,620
Yes, Father?

182
00:09:41,240 --> 00:09:43,360
That gun there beside you,
pick it up.

183
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:45,580
Uh...O-okay?

184
00:09:47,990 --> 00:09:51,100
Now, child, I want you to shoot
the Fullmetal Alchemist.

185
00:09:51,140 --> 00:09:52,320
[GASPS]

186
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:54,960
No, I...
Father I can't do that!

187
00:09:55,080 --> 00:10:00,200
I am the Sun God's chosen emissary.
My word is the word of Leto himself.

188
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:03,380
Shoot him, Rose.
It's God's will.

189
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:05,960
[SHAKY BREATHING]

190
00:10:06,010 --> 00:10:07,240
Why hesitate?

191
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:10,500
When you lost your fiance
to that tragic accident last year,

192
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:14,080
who was it that saved you
from the very depths of despair?

193
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:16,080
Have you forgotten?

194
00:10:17,180 --> 00:10:18,840
[VOICE TREMBLING]
It was you, Father.

195
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:22,520
That's right. It was I who took your
hand and lead you into God's light.

196
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:24,940
And do you recall what it was
I promised you then?

197
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:27,580
You said if I had faith
you'd bring him back to life!

198
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:32,460
No, wait!
It's not me, honest!

199
00:10:32,460 --> 00:10:33,700
[GASP]

200
00:10:34,290 --> 00:10:36,200
Dammit,
I'm the Fullmetal Alchemist!

201
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:38,180
It's not him!
It's me!

202
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:40,320
It's the short one?!
You're kidding!

203
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:44,840
I'm sorry, but I...
I have to do this...

204
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:46,200
I don't have any choice.

205
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:48,020
ED: He's been lying to you, Rose.

206
00:10:48,020 --> 00:10:49,800
You're wrong!
I've seen his miracles!

207
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:52,390
Father Cornello will bring
him back to life, I have faith!

208
00:10:52,640 --> 00:10:53,800
Fine, then shoot.

209
00:11:00,060 --> 00:11:01,190
Al!

210
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:05,420
[SHRIEKS]

211
00:11:05,490 --> 00:11:08,440
Good. God Leto is pleased,
you have done well, my child.

212
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:10,860
Now pick up the gun and
shoot the other as well.

213
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:13,830
Haven't you made her do
enough already?

214
00:11:13,910 --> 00:11:14,910
[GASPS]

215
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:17,450
But...your head...!
I thought you were...

216
00:11:17,540 --> 00:11:19,300
Don't worry about it,
he's pretty solid.

217
00:11:19,300 --> 00:11:21,140
Yeah, see?
No harm done.

218
00:11:23,090 --> 00:11:25,700
An empty suit of armor that
walks and speaks!

219
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:27,540
Do you still doubt it, Rose?

220
00:11:27,540 --> 00:11:29,640
This unholy thing is an abomination!

221
00:11:29,660 --> 00:11:31,840
Evil of this kind must be purged!

222
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:37,040
[GROWLING]

223
00:11:37,120 --> 00:11:40,240
And I believe my Chimera
should be up to the task.

224
00:11:40,980 --> 00:11:44,740
So this is the sorta thing you do with
a Philosopher's Stone? That's just twisted.

225
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:45,920
[GASP]

226
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:49,990
Anyway, looks like I'll need a weapon.

227
00:11:56,620 --> 00:11:58,520
No transmutation circle?!

228
00:11:58,560 --> 00:12:02,240
So the State Alchemist title
isn't just for show, you truly are gifted.

229
00:12:02,260 --> 00:12:03,540
However...!

230
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:05,540
[CHIMERA ROARS]

231
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:11,720
Your little spear is no match for
Chimera claws that tear through iron!

232
00:12:12,640 --> 00:12:14,760
You shredded my pants.

233
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:20,540
But I guess those claws don't do
so good against steel!

234
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:22,640
Bite him, you stupid beast!

235
00:12:25,980 --> 00:12:30,500
You like that, kitty?
Go on, get a good taste!

236
00:12:35,060 --> 00:12:36,580
Your arm...

237
00:12:36,600 --> 00:12:38,740
A brother trapped in armor...

238
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:41,860
I see. It's all
becoming clear now.

239
00:12:42,340 --> 00:12:43,980
You did it, didn't you?

240
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:48,170
The one thing even the most novice
alchemist knows is strictly forbidden!

241
00:12:48,250 --> 00:12:50,210
Why don't you come down
here and try me?

242
00:12:50,300 --> 00:12:52,860
I'll show you real quick
who the novice is!

243
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:55,060
Fullmetal Alchemist.

244
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,780
Fullmetal Alchemist.

245
00:12:59,600 --> 00:13:01,420
Why don't you come down
here and try me?

246
00:13:01,420 --> 00:13:03,800
I'll show you real quick
who the novice is!

247
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:06,460
Rose...
this is the price of their sin.

248
00:13:06,460 --> 00:13:08,880
These fools attempted
human transmutation,

249
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:11,280
the greatest taboo
for any alchemist!

250
00:13:11,660 --> 00:13:15,440
In their arrogance, they tried to
bring someone dead back to life.

251
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:22,600
He thought he could touch the sun, but when he got too close
his wings melted and he came crashing back down to Earth.

252
00:13:23,330 --> 00:13:24,660
Oh, no...

253
00:13:24,750 --> 00:13:28,980
This is what happens when you try to
play God, or whatever you wanna call it.

254
00:13:29,170 --> 00:13:32,380
Take a good look, Rose.
Is this what you want?

255
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:38,460
So this is the great Fullmetal Alchemist,
Edward Elric, not even half a man.

256
00:13:38,460 --> 00:13:39,920
Hell, not even half a boy!

257
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:41,360
And what are you?!

258
00:13:41,380 --> 00:13:44,620
You're just a phony that can't do
anything without a Philosopher's Stone!

259
00:13:44,620 --> 00:13:48,270
Father, we just want you to hand
over the Stone before you get hurt.

260
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:49,960
Don't be absurd!

261
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:52,580
Why? So you could use it
for yourself? Please.

262
00:13:52,740 --> 00:13:57,440
If you fools are really so eager to play God,
then perhaps I should send you to meet him instead!

263
00:14:01,280 --> 00:14:01,960
Huh?

264
00:14:02,290 --> 00:14:05,480
Nah, me and God,
we don't get along too well.

265
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:08,940
Even if I went, he'd probably
just send me right back here.

266
00:14:12,580 --> 00:14:14,170
[ROSE SCREAMS]

267
00:14:14,170 --> 00:14:15,090
This way!

268
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:24,540
Well don't just stand there!
After them!

269
00:14:24,560 --> 00:14:27,940
These heathens seek to harm the order!
They must be stopped!

270
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:32,120
That's far enough.

271
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:34,720
What are you gonna do, boy?
You're unarmed and outnumbered.

272
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:37,860
Look, just come quietly.
We don't wanna have to rough you up.

273
00:14:38,380 --> 00:14:39,320
Ha ha ha ha!

274
00:14:41,160 --> 00:14:41,740
Huh?!

275
00:14:41,740 --> 00:14:43,480
[ALL SCREAMING]

276
00:14:44,790 --> 00:14:47,040
Don't go easy just 'cause
he's a kid, you got that?

277
00:14:47,830 --> 00:14:49,670
[YELLING]

278
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:52,620
[ED CACKLING]

279
00:14:53,590 --> 00:14:55,960
AL: What do you think of
Cornello now, Rose?

280
00:14:57,050 --> 00:15:00,160
He just opened fire, he didn't
care that you were in the way.

281
00:15:00,180 --> 00:15:02,390
But...that's because...

282
00:15:05,140 --> 00:15:07,460
What he said back there
is true, isn't it?

283
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:13,740
We're not evil. All we wanted was
to see our mom smile again.

284
00:15:14,660 --> 00:15:17,360
But our transmutation failed.

285
00:15:17,450 --> 00:15:20,660
What we made...
wasn't even human.

286
00:15:22,820 --> 00:15:25,180
We learned our
mistake the hard way.

287
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:29,040
People don't come back
from the dead. Not ever.

288
00:15:29,330 --> 00:15:31,370
That's not true!
I mean...

289
00:15:31,460 --> 00:15:34,670
Alchemy is based on
the law of equivalent exchange.

290
00:15:34,750 --> 00:15:38,660
The price of even a failed
human transmutation was enormous.

291
00:15:39,140 --> 00:15:44,320
It cost my brother his left leg,
and it cost me my whole body.

292
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:48,820
Do you see it?
My brother drew that with his own blood.

293
00:15:49,380 --> 00:15:50,440
[GASP]

294
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:55,720
His leg had been taken, he was bleeding,
I can't imagine the pain he was in...

295
00:15:55,820 --> 00:15:59,860
But through all that he still gave up his
right arm to transmute my soul...

296
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:02,540
and bonded me
to this suit of armor.

297
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:08,300
Now, I just want to help him get his
body back to the way it was.

298
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:11,960
He wants to find a way to get
me back to normal, too.

299
00:16:12,140 --> 00:16:15,800
It won't be easy.
We might even get killed along the way.

300
00:16:16,820 --> 00:16:20,920
But that's the path we chose.
All we can do is keep moving.

301
00:16:21,010 --> 00:16:23,680
But, Father Cornello said...

302
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:24,740
[GASP]

303
00:16:25,390 --> 00:16:27,340
He said he could do it,
he promised me!

304
00:16:27,340 --> 00:16:30,020
Just because you and your brother
failed that doesn't mean...

305
00:16:30,220 --> 00:16:31,770
It doesn't mean he will!

306
00:16:34,770 --> 00:16:36,780
There you are,
you infernal brat!

307
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:39,480
Look, can we just cut
the crap and talk here?

308
00:16:39,570 --> 00:16:42,860
All I want are some straight
answers about the Stone.

309
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:46,040
Tell me what I need to know,
and I'll be on my way.

310
00:16:46,220 --> 00:16:48,160
Or we could get the
military involved...?

311
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:52,660
Ask your questions.

312
00:16:52,750 --> 00:16:55,480
You could do anything with a
Philosopher's Stone, right?

313
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:58,680
So why waste all that power
performing phony miracles?

314
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:03,320
Because with each miracle I can attract
new believers to the order.

315
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:06,160
Believers who would
lay down their lives for my sake!

316
00:17:06,300 --> 00:17:08,040
I'm slowly building an army...

317
00:17:08,040 --> 00:17:10,940
A legion of holy warriors,
unafraid to die!

318
00:17:11,260 --> 00:17:15,540
In a few more years, I'll be ready to unleash
this mindless horde upon the world!

319
00:17:15,620 --> 00:17:19,020
And I'll use the Philosopher's Stone
to tear this country apart.

320
00:17:19,260 --> 00:17:22,380
Who knows?
I might even carve out a slice for you.

321
00:17:22,380 --> 00:17:23,840
[CACKLING]

322
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:27,560
[ED JOINS LAUGHING]
CORNELLO: Wait, what are you  laughing about?

323
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:30,760
I knew it! You really
are a novice, aren't you?

324
00:17:37,210 --> 00:17:38,140
[GASPS]

325
00:17:38,220 --> 00:17:40,560
You don't mean that—?!

326
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:43,300
There were never
any miracles, Rose.

327
00:17:43,300 --> 00:17:45,860
He lied to you.
He lied to everyone.

328
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:48,120
CORNELLO: Why, you...!

329
00:17:48,120 --> 00:17:50,480
How long?!
How long has that been on?!

330
00:17:50,890 --> 00:17:52,140
ED: From the start!

331
00:17:52,220 --> 00:17:54,140
Your believers heard every word.

332
00:17:54,230 --> 00:17:56,020
CORNELLO: How could you?!

333
00:17:56,360 --> 00:17:58,360
You'll pay dearly for this!

334
00:17:59,190 --> 00:18:00,980
Sorry, not today!

335
00:18:02,610 --> 00:18:05,380
Just face it,
you're outclassed here.

336
00:18:07,660 --> 00:18:09,570
I am without rival!

337
00:18:18,940 --> 00:18:20,620
I-It's a rebound!

338
00:18:20,640 --> 00:18:23,380
No! I won't be disgraced like this!

339
00:18:23,700 --> 00:18:26,440
Now boy... behold...

340
00:18:26,460 --> 00:18:29,860
[VOICE DISTORTING]
...the chosen emissary of the Sun God Leto!

341
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:55,250
My word is the divine word of God himself!
My fist is the almighty fist of judgement!

342
00:18:55,620 --> 00:18:56,860
Oh yeah?

343
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,860
Fist of God, huh?

344
00:19:00,400 --> 00:19:02,960
Well if that's what you want,
you can have it!

345
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:20,560
[GROANING]

346
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:22,060
Shut up!

347
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:24,580
Just give me the
Philosopher's Stone!

348
00:19:29,560 --> 00:19:31,080
What the hell...?

349
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:32,950
The Stone...

350
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:37,040
It's supposed to be perfect material...
How did it just break like that?!

351
00:19:37,240 --> 00:19:40,160
I-I don't know.
I don't know anything about it!

352
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:43,560
S-Spare me! Please! I-I was wrong!
Please, I beg you!

353
00:19:43,560 --> 00:19:45,200
It's a damn fake.

354
00:19:45,200 --> 00:19:49,040
Please, don't! I'm helpless without
the Stone. Spare me, please!

355
00:19:49,040 --> 00:19:50,740
You mean we
went through all this...

356
00:19:50,740 --> 00:19:53,260
Risked our lives for this
one possible chance...

357
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:55,720
and it's a fake?!

358
00:19:55,820 --> 00:19:58,580
So u-uh...
what about me?

359
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:02,400
I don't care what you do,
just get outta here!

360
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:03,400
Right!

361
00:20:06,260 --> 00:20:08,030
AL: And what about the Stone?

362
00:20:08,110 --> 00:20:10,610
ED: Phony, just like him.

363
00:20:10,700 --> 00:20:11,740
AL: Oh.

364
00:20:13,070 --> 00:20:16,880
I'm sorry, Al. For awhile there I thought
we'd really found a way to get your body back.

365
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:19,460
ROSE: Give me the Philosopher's Stone!

366
00:20:20,080 --> 00:20:21,480
AL: Rose...

367
00:20:22,580 --> 00:20:25,960
Like I was just saying, it was a fake.
It wasn't real.

368
00:20:26,240 --> 00:20:28,020
Besides, it's shattered now.

369
00:20:28,020 --> 00:20:30,780
Liar! You wanna keep it for
yourself, don't you?!

370
00:20:31,090 --> 00:20:33,760
So you can use it on your bodies!
That's right!

371
00:20:33,760 --> 00:20:36,140
And so you can try to bring
your mother back again!

372
00:20:36,160 --> 00:20:37,700
You shut up!

373
00:20:38,220 --> 00:20:42,300
People don't come back from
the dead, Rose. Not ever.

374
00:20:44,060 --> 00:20:45,520
Not ever.

375
00:20:47,560 --> 00:20:49,860
But he promised me...

376
00:20:50,360 --> 00:20:52,740
He said if I prayed it
would happen...

377
00:20:52,780 --> 00:20:54,880
[CRYING]
...a miracle...

378
00:20:56,180 --> 00:21:00,440
That hope was all I had left,
what am I supposed to believe in now?!

379
00:21:00,980 --> 00:21:02,910
Tell me what to do!

380
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:05,200
Please!

381
00:21:06,980 --> 00:21:10,320
I can't tell you that,
you have to figure it out.

382
00:21:11,920 --> 00:21:16,020
Stand up and walk.
Keep moving forward.

383
00:21:16,540 --> 00:21:19,320
You've got two good legs,
so use them.

384
00:21:20,420 --> 00:21:23,060
You're strong enough to
make your own path.

385
00:21:29,680 --> 00:21:33,100
Bring him out here!
We're through listening to those lies!

386
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:36,180
Show yourself! Just get out here!
Open up!

387
00:21:37,990 --> 00:21:40,820
That damn brat, it's all all ruined!
Everything I worked for!

388
00:21:40,830 --> 00:21:42,980
Yes, all that hard work for nothing.

389
00:21:42,980 --> 00:21:43,540
Huh?!

390
00:21:43,540 --> 00:21:46,370
I knew we should've just
incited a little rebellion.

391
00:21:47,220 --> 00:21:48,060
You...!

392
00:21:48,080 --> 00:21:51,840
I'm hungry, Lust, can I eat the old man?
Please, he's big and fat!

393
00:21:51,840 --> 00:21:56,100
Not this one, Gluttony.
We don't want you giving yourself indigestion.

394
00:21:56,340 --> 00:21:58,620
Now you too?
Everyone has mocked me!

395
00:21:58,620 --> 00:22:00,240
I won't stand for—

396
00:22:04,840 --> 00:22:07,650
I'd say this concludes
our business.

397
00:22:11,980 --> 00:22:14,780
Just as things were beginning
to look promising, too.

398
00:22:14,780 --> 00:22:17,360
Now I suppose we'll have to
start over from scratch.

399
00:22:18,100 --> 00:22:19,880
Father won't be pleased.

400
00:22:20,180 --> 00:22:24,240
In any case, it's time we started
thinking about our next move.

401
00:22:26,660 --> 00:22:27,740
[CRUNCH]

402
00:22:28,380 --> 00:22:34,200
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

403
00:22:34,280 --> 00:22:39,500
nee kimi wa oboete imasu ka

404
00:22:39,560 --> 00:22:45,260
Yakusoku chigiri shoka
no kaze ga tsutsumu

405
00:22:45,520 --> 00:22:50,400
futari yorisotta

406
00:22:53,480 --> 00:22:58,660
Muri na egao no ura

407
00:22:58,660 --> 00:23:04,040
nobita kage o kakumau

408
00:23:04,080 --> 00:23:13,420
Dakara kizukanu furi saisei o erabu

409
00:23:15,500 --> 00:23:22,640
Table no ue no furuenai shirase machitsuzukete

410
00:23:26,060 --> 00:23:31,480
kuuhaku no yoru o kuru hazu no nai asa mo

411
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:35,780
zenbu wakatte'tan da

412
00:23:35,860 --> 00:23:41,340
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

413
00:23:41,340 --> 00:23:46,540
nee itsuka omoidasu deshou

414
00:23:46,540 --> 00:23:51,980
Hatasenakatta yakusoku o idaite

415
00:23:52,220 --> 00:23:57,040
futari arukidasu

416
00:24:00,840 --> 00:24:06,760
Following the incident in Liore, Ed and Al travel to
the Eastern Command Center to report to Colonel Mustang.

417
00:24:06,820 --> 00:24:11,380
Once there, they are taken to the home
of the Sewing Life Alchemist, Shou Tucker,

418
00:24:11,400 --> 00:24:16,000
and his young daughter, Nina, where they hope
to learn more about the field of bio-alchemy.

419
00:24:16,400 --> 00:24:19,460
Next time on Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

420
00:24:19,500 --> 00:24:22,940
Episode 4: An Alchemist's Anguish

421
00:24:23,700 --> 00:24:27,870
Some meetings in this life
are destined only for heartbreak.
